fixed 13 exact_finite_decision type audit (2026-08-17)

Method
  The manifest is an audit target, not controlling evidence. Every contract was read in the
  fixed order: Lean binders -> full proposition/return type and direction -> Julia signature
  and output -> quantified coverage -> trust boundary. Complete finite enumeration was used
  only after proposition and codomain agreement had been established.

Decision summary
  Retain exact_finite_decision: 8.
  Reject exact_finite_decision under the current binding: 5.
  The two theory-invariant contracts, hinge.act and body.no_terminal_setpoint, retain exact;
  no theory-invariant downgrade stop is triggered.

RETAIN EXACT

1. interface.relation_linearization -- ACCEPT exact.
   Lean: formal/ERIEC/InterfaceLinearization.lean:47,
   convSystem_linearization_eq_adjoint, concludes equality of the converse incidence
   linearization and adjoint. Julia: src/interface_linearization.jl:14 computes both complete
   finite incidence matrices and compares sigma with transpose(alpha). Over real 0/1 incidence
   matrices this independently decides the conclusion; complete M/E carriers cover every
   matrix entry. Relation functions are candidate data, not obligation oracles.

2. interface.relation_naturality -- ACCEPT exact.
   Lean: InterfaceLinearization.lean:82, RelationIso binder and reindexed matrix equality.
   Julia: interface_linearization.jl:28 validates both carrier bijections, map_iff over every
   source pair, and the complete reindexed incidence equality. All RelationIso obligations and
   the conclusion are recomputed from candidate maps and relations.

3. interface.relation_lax_naturality -- ACCEPT exact.
   Lean: InterfaceLinearization.lean:103, the pointwise 0/1 matrix inequality induced by a
   RelationHom. Julia: interface_linearization.jl:60 exhausts every supplied domain/codomain
   pair and evaluates exactly the equivalent implication rel(m,e) -> rel'(f m,g e).

4. hinge.act -- ACCEPT exact after the user-directed strict rebind.
   Lean: formal/ERIEC/Hinge.lean:17, ActNonempty : Prop. Julia: src/hinge.jl:9 returns exactly
   !isempty(Act(...)). The former Set/Bool codomain mismatch was removed without weakening M3.
   Relation functions are the supplied object data and the intersection is recomputed.

5. decomp.copair_unique -- ACCEPT exact.
   Lean: formal/ERIEC/Decomp.lean:12, candidate = copair under both component equations.
   Julia: src/decomp.jl:4 exhausts the complete supplied A and B carriers, hence every Sum A B
   input, and checks both component equations and the conclusion. The candidate functions are
   data and no proof Bool is accepted.

6. graded.presheaf_transition_naturality -- ACCEPT exact.
   Lean: formal/ERIEC/Graded.lean:135, naturality for every tag, comparable u/v, and x in the
   source fiber. Julia: src/graded.jl:415 first validates both finite presheaves and transition
   outputs, then exhausts all transitions, object pairs, and complete source fibers. Component,
   restriction, and order functions are candidate data; the naturality equality is recomputed.

7. body.no_terminal_setpoint -- ACCEPT exact.
   Lean: formal/ERIEC/Body.lean:87, NoTerminalSetPoint is the negation of existence of an object
   reached from every source. Julia: src/body.jl:157 exhausts every candidate and every source in
   the duplicate-free complete object carrier. reaches is the diagram relation itself, not a
   proof callback. The M4b invariant remains unchanged.

8. richness.branch -- ACCEPT exact.
   Lean: formal/ERIEC/Richness.lean:8, existence of two distinct values in alphaRel m.
   Julia: src/richness.jl:11 forms the complete finite image and checks every pair for distinct
   witnesses. The relation image is candidate data and the existential is independently decided.

REJECT EXACT UNDER CURRENT BINDING

9. interface.sensitivity_realization -- REVISE.
   Lean: InterfaceLinearization.lean:63, converse_linearization_eq_sensitivity_adjoint assumes
   both a ConvSystem and hRealizes, then concludes an equality involving sigma and the sensitivity
   adjoint. Julia: interface_linearization.jl:21 receives no sigma/ConvSystem and checks only
   Jacobian(response,base) = incidence(alpha), the hRealizes premise. It does not decide the bound
   theorem conclusion. Minimal strict correction: bind the contract to the existing
   ERIEC.InterfaceLinearization.RealizesSensitivityAt definition and then re-audit exactness;
   otherwise exact must be removed. This binding change is a user decision.

10. grading.const_presheaf_antitone -- REVISE.
    Lean: formal/ERIEC/Grading.lean:28, constPresheaf_iff_antitone is an Iff between existence of
    a RelPresheaf and AntitoneRelation. Julia: src/grading.jl:2 decides only AntitoneRelation on
    complete carriers. It does not decide the Iff proposition (which the theorem proves) or encode
    the existential structure. Minimal strict correction: bind to the existing
    ERIEC.Grading.AntitoneRelation definition; otherwise exact must be removed. User decision.

11. certification.critical_bound -- ACCEPT downgrade, REVISE its condition.
    Lean: formal/ERIEC/DC.lean:52, crit_bound assumes global sig2, K.Nonempty, and post-fixedness,
    then concludes not threshold<rank. Julia: src/dc.jl:157 checks the local implication for one
    rank and one K, and never validates global sig2 or all configurations. It is not exact.
    complete_only is valid only with a manifest assumption that the supplied local instance is
    drawn from a faithful Lean witness satisfying sig2; a faithful full witness necessarily
    passes this projection, while acceptance alone cannot establish sig2.

12. invariance.update_bisimulation -- CHALLENGE complete_only; use regression_only.
    Lean: formal/ERIEC/Invariance/Dynamic.lean:19, upd_bisim names mapConf/upd and assumes hPhi,
    hTheta, and DriftEquivariant before concluding equality for c. Julia: src/invariance.jl:2
    accepts arbitrary map/update/update_prime callbacks and a non-exhaustive sample list. There is
    no bridge binding them to mapConf/upd or the three hypotheses. Therefore Lean theorem truth
    does not imply acceptance of arbitrary Julia callbacks: even the complete_only direction is
    unproved. Current safe classification is regression_only.

13. temporaldc.observed_termination -- REJECT exact; regression_only until redesigned.
    Lean: formal/ERIEC/TemporalDC.lean:179, ObservedTerminationStep O x y is a proposition for one
    explicit pair x,y and includes T.next x y. Julia: src/temporal_dc.jl:32 receives a Boolean
    linear trace and mask, assumes vector adjacency represents next, and returns whether there
    exists any observed true-to-false adjacent pair. A pointwise pair predicate and an existential
    search over a runtime prefix are different propositions. No existing Lean existential trace
    predicate is bound to the checker. Use regression_only unless a user-approved Lean predicate
    or an explicit endpoint checker restores proposition identity.

Consequences if all recommendations are adopted
  Immediate downgrades: critical_bound, update_bisimulation, observed_termination.
  Exact-preserving rebind candidates requiring user decisions: sensitivity_realization to
  RealizesSensitivityAt; const_presheaf_antitone to AntitoneRelation.
  Exact count would fall from 29 to 26 after the three immediate downgrades, while the two strict
  rebinds could remain exact after their own audits. The sensitivity registry must delete the
  downgraded IDs and update its SHA-256 in the same implementation batch. No manifest, registry,
  source, test, gate, commit, or push change was made by this audit.
